ocument states that it \\\"\n \\\"performs heartbeating concurrently with other AppendEntries RPCs 'to avoid having to set the election timeout high enough to account for the \\\"\n \\\"max acceptable disk operation' (docs/divergence.md:25-34), so the term update must remain correct under exactly this overlap.\\\")\njson.dump({'rationale':(\\\"Add document anchors read this turn: the membership document's definition of a non-voter and its statement that a new configuration \\\"\n  \\\"takes effect only once appended to the log, and the divergence document's declared concurrent heartbeating. They tighten the VerifyLeader, \\\"\n  \\\"phantom-configuration and heartbeat accounts respectively; no evidence or conclusion changes.\\\"),\n 'sources':[\n  {'id':'membership_doc_defs','file':'membership.md','start_line':11,'end_line':15,'kind':'document_statement'},\n  {'id':'membership_doc_nonvoter','file':'membership.md','start_line':11,'end_line':12,'kind':'document_statement'},\n  {'id':'divergence_async_heartbeats','file':'docs/divergence.md','start_line':25,'end_line':34,'kind':'document_statement'}],\n 'interpretations':[phn,vfn,hbn]},open('draft/update.json','w'),indent=2)\nprint('ok')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-17_17-50-22-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
